According to a report by IntelMarketResearch, the global Livestock Management App Market was valued at USD 157 million in 2025 and is projected to reach USD 293 million by 2034, registering a CAGR of 9.4% during 2025–2034. The market is being shaped by rapid digital transformation across agriculture, widespread smartphone adoption on farms, increasing demand for livestock products, growing use of precision livestock technologies, regulatory requirements for traceability, and rising emphasis on animal health and sustainability.
Livestock management apps provide farmers, ranchers, veterinarians and agribusinesses with digital tools for monitoring animal health, managing breeding cycles, optimizing feed and nutrition, tracking herd performance and supporting financial and operational decisions. By bringing multiple farm-management functions into a single digital interface, these platforms can reduce dependence on manual records and support faster, data-driven decisions.
